{"step_index":2438,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:45:28Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-27T16:15:28+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-27T16:15:29+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_problems.js`\nTotal Lines: 13801\nTotal Bytes: 727252\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: // app_build/dsa_problems.js — 300 Curated, Distinct LeetCode & DSA Problems\r\n2: // Phase 3: Structured Catalog with Verified Source URLs, Constraints, Prerequisites, and Reference Solutions\r\n3: window.DSA_PROBLEMS_LIBRARY = [\r\n4:   {\r\n5:     \"id\": 1,\r\n6:     \"leetcodeNumber\": 1,\r\n7:     \"title\": \"Two Sum\",\r\n8:     \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\r\n9:     \"topic\": \"Arrays & Hashing\",\r\n10:     \"pattern\": \"Hash Map Lookup\",\r\n11:     \"description\": \"Find indices of two numbers that add up to a target using a dictionary for instant lookups.\",\r\n12:     \"timeComplexity\": \"O(n)\",\r\n13:     \"spaceComplexity\": \"O(n)\",\r\n14:     \"starterCode\": \"def twoSum(nums, target):\\n    prevMap = {}\\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\\n        diff = target - nums[i]\\n        if diff in prevMap:\\n            return [prevMap[diff], i]\\n        prevMap[nums[i]] = i\\n    return []\\n\\nnums = [2, 7, 11, 15]\\nprint(\\\"Indices:\\\", twoSum(nums, 9))\",\r\n15:     \"topics\": [\r\n16:       \"Arrays\",\r\n17:       \"Hashing and Hash Maps\",\r\n18:       \"Math and Number Theory\",\r\n19:       \"Recursion\"\r\n20:     ],\r\n21:     \"sourceUrl\": \"https://leetcode.com/problems/two-sum/\",\r\n22:     \"primaryTopic\": \"Arrays & Hashing\",\r\n23:     \"topicTags\": [\r\n24:       \"Arrays\",\r\n25:       \"Hashing and Hash Maps\",\r\n26:       \"Math and Number Theory\",\r\n27:       \"Recursion\"\r\n28:     ],\r\n29:     \"summary\": \"Find indices of two numbers that add up to a target using a dictionary for instant lookups.\",\r\n30:     \"examples\": [\r\n31:       {\r\n32:         \"input\": \"nums = [2, 7, 11, 15]\",\r\n33:         \"output\": \"Computed via twoSum(nums, 9)\",\r\n34:         \"explanation\": \"Step through the execution in the visualizer to inspect how variables mutate to produce the result.\"\r\n35:       }\r\n36:     ],\r\n37:     \"constraints\": [\r\n38:       \"1 <= nums.length <= 10^4\",\r\n39:       \"-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4\",\r\n40:       \"Memory limit: 256 MB, Time limit: 2.0 seconds\"\r\n41:     ],\r\n42:     \"prerequisites\": [\r\n43:       \"Array Indexing & Iteration\",\r\n44:       \"Hash Map / Dict Key Lookup\",\r\n45:       \"Recursive Call Stack & Base Cases\"\r\n46:     ],\r\n47:     \"referenceSolution\": \"def twoSum(nums, target):\\n    prevMap = {}\\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\\n        diff = target - nums[i]\\n        if diff in prevMap:\\n            return [prevMap[diff], i]\\n        prevMap[nums[i]] = i\\n    return []\\n\\nnums = [2, 7, 11, 15]\\nprint(\\\"Indices:\\\", twoSum(nums, 9))\",\r\n48:     \"verificationStatus\": \"Verified\"\r\n49:   },\r\n50:   {\r\n51:     \"id\": 2,\r\n52:     \"leetcodeNumber\": 217,\r\n53:     \"title\": \"Contains Duplicate\",\r\n54:     \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\r\n55:     \"topic\": \"Arrays & Hashing\",\r\n56:     \"pattern\": \"Hash Set\",\r\n57:     \"description\": \"Determine if any value appears at least twice in the array using a set.\",\r\n58:     \"timeComplexity\": \"O(n)\",\r\n59:     \"spaceComplexity\": \"O(n)\",\r\n60:     \"starterCode\": \"def containsDuplicate(nums):\\n    seen = set()\\n    for n in nums:\\n        if n in seen:\\n            return True\\n        seen.add(n)\\n    return False\\n\\nprint(\\\"Has duplicate:\\\", containsDuplicate([1, 2, 3, 1]))\",\r\nThe above content