{"step_index":2465,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:49:36Z","input_tokens":2798,"cache_read_tokens":187086,"output_tokens":12176,"thinking":"This mapping neatly categorizes the problem IDs by their core algorithmic techniques.  The initial focus will be on the Arrays & Hashing group, given its prevalence. Proceeding from there, the Bit Manipulation and Two Pointers approaches will be considered if necessary.\n\n\nThe problem IDs have been cross-referenced and the canonical IDs are now confirmed, resolving the ID ambiguity. The association between problem IDs and their corresponding algorithmic techniques is validated for future reference. The data has been aligned to ensure accurate problem identification.\n\n\nThe plan is to populate the solution registry with both baseline and optimized approaches for canonical problems, including detailed explanations and complexity analysis. Each of the remaining problems in the catalog will receive a designated optimized solution. The initial focus is providing complete solutions with detailed explanations for a smaller subset of problems.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# scratch/generate_phase6_solutions_data.py\\nimport json\\nimport os\\n\\nwith open('app_build/dsa_problems.js', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n    text = f.read()\\n\\nstart_idx = text.find('[')\\nend_idx = text.rfind(']')\\nproblems = json.loads(text[start_idx:end_idx + 1])\\nprint(f\\\"Loaded {len(problems)} problems\\\")\\n\\n# Complete Dual Approaches (Baseline vs Optimized) for 20+ Canonical Problems\\nDUAL_APPROACHES = {\\n    # 1. Two Sum (LC 1, ID 1)\\n    1: {\\n        \\\"hasMultipleApproaches\\\": True,\\n        \\\"approaches\\\": [\\n            {\\n                \\\"id\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\\n                \\\"name\\\": \\\"Approach 1: Brute Force (Baseline)\\\",\\n                \\\"isBaseline\\\": True,\\n                \\\"timeComplexity\\\": \\\"O(n²)\\\",\\n                \\\"spaceComplexity\\\": \\\"O(1)\\\",\\n                \\\"code\\\": \\\"def twoSum(nums, target):\\\\n    n = len(nums)\\\\n    for i in range(n):\\\\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\\\\n            if nums[i] + nums[j] == target:\\\\n                return [i, j]\\\\n    return []\\\\n\\\\nnums = [2, 7, 11, 15]\\\\nprint(\\\\\\\"Indices:\\\\\\\", twoSum(nums, 9))\\\",\\n                \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"Iterate through every possible pair of elements using nested loops. For each pair (i, j) where j > i, check if their sum equals target. Return their indices immediately upon finding a match.\\\",\\n                \\\"whyItWorks\\\": \\\"Exhaustively checks every unique unordered pair (i, j) with i < j. If any valid pair exists that sums to target, this search space is guaranteed to find it.\\\",\\n                \\\"commonMistakes\\\": [\\n                    \\\"Starting the inner loop at j = 0 or j = i instead of j = i + 1, which accidentally reuses the same element twice.\\\",\\n                    \\\"Time limit exceeded (TLE) on large arrays: n² operations exceed the execution limit when n = 10,000.\\\",\\n                    \\\"Returning values [nums[i], nums[j]] instead of indices [i, j].\\\"\\n                ],\\n                \\\"isVerified\\\": True\\n            },\\n            {\\n                \\\"id\\\": \\\"optimized\\\",\\n           \n<truncated 40842 bytes>","Description":"\"Script to generate complete Phase 6 solutions registry\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CVT\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef\\\\scratch\\\\generate_phase6_solutions_data.py\"","toolAction":"\"Writing Phase 6 solutions generator\"","toolSummary":"\"Create generate_phase6_solutions_data.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
